        "title": "Quantitative Finance - Field Map and Orientation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Finance is applied mathematics: stochastic calculus, optimization, statistics, and\nprobability theory deployed on market data. As an MIT Math + TCS person, you already have\nthe machinery — this maps it onto the financial domain and shows where the interesting\nmathematical problems live."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#003",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:finance:00-overview, git-history:finance:00-overview]",
