        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "finance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Quantitative Finance - Field Map and Orientation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Adverse selection:** Market makers face traders with private information (informed\ntraders). The bid-ask spread compensates for the risk of trading against someone who\nknows the stock is worth $110 when you're selling at $100.05. This is the Kyle (1985)\nand Glosten-Milgrom (1985) framework."
    },
